Subject: [PATCH 0/2] thunderbolt: stream: Fixes for Falcon Ridge hosts

Hi,

USB4STREAM wedges the Falcon Ridge 4C host routers in a Mac Pro 6,1:
after a stream's Tx ring has run with end-to-end flow control, the
router stops answering config reads until the NHI is reset. This is the
failure commit 1881f2efbf7f fixed in thunderbolt_net; patch 1 does the
same for USB4STREAM by keeping E2E only on the Rx ring.

Patch 2 fixes HopID bookkeeping we noticed while recovering from that:
HopIDs that failed to allocate when a stream attached were released
later anyway, which warned in ida_free.

Patch 1's change was tested on a Mac Pro 6,1 (three Falcon Ridge 4C
controllers cabled to each other, software connection manager) running
7.2.9: streams carry data both ways (64-byte round trips of 25 us,
9.6 Gb/s one way per cable, 15.9 Gb/s across three cables at once) and
no config read times out. Patch 2 is compile-tested only, on 7.2.9. The
series applies to next-20261006 but was not built there.

Tom Fairfield (2):
  thunderbolt: stream: Don't use end-to-end flow control on the Tx ring
  thunderbolt: stream: Don't release HopIDs that were never allocated

 drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

